{#
  1.39 (tree.context_menu): the «…» button of a page tree row (UiKit tree `actions_template`, WikiTreeMenu), the touch
  way to the row's menu. Hidden until wiki.js finds an entry the user may take on that row; out of the tab order
  (tabindex -1), as UiKit asks, so the tree keeps one tab stop: the keyboard opens the same menu with the ContextMenu
  key or Shift+F10 on the row. It keeps its place in the row whether shown or not (visibility), so nothing moves.
  No aria-expanded (the UiKit tree reads [aria-expanded=true] as an unfolded parent); data-wiki-open marks the open menu.
  aria-hidden: a tree may only own tree items and groups (axe aria-required-children), so the button is a pointer and
  touch affordance only; assistive technologies reach the same menu from the row with Shift+F10 / the ContextMenu key.
  Variables: node (UiKit tree node: id, label, item_attr).
#}
{% trans_default_domain 'NowoWikiBundle' %}
<button type="button" class="nowo-wiki-tree__more" tabindex="-1" hidden aria-hidden="true" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-controls="nowo-wiki-tree-menu" aria-label="{{ 'wiki.tree_menu.more'|trans({'%title%': node.label|nowo_ui_trans}) }}" title="{{ 'wiki.tree_menu.more'|trans({'%title%': node.label|nowo_ui_trans}) }}" data-wiki-tree-menu-more data-testid="wiki-tree-menu-more"><span aria-hidden="true">…</span></button>
